WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.632
This slide focuses on Two-dimensional arrays Start
with the data structure and what

00:00:05.658 --> 00:00:11.603
the operation is supposed to accomplish before
looking closely at the syntax A

00:00:11.617 --> 00:00:17.540
2-D array looks like a table of numbers Axis 0
usually means down columns

00:00:18.474 --> 00:00:26.061
Axis 1 usually means across rows Rows columns and
axes Before

00:00:26.087 --> 00:00:31.642
running the example predict the structure and output
Run it in the browser inspect the

00:00:31.669 --> 00:00:37.761
values dimensions labels or summary then change one
input and run it again Focus

00:00:37.787 --> 00:00:41.827
on how the operation changes the data rather than
reading the code line by line
